Files changed since then say so in their header.

laya-r-mlx's NOTICE, kept as required:

  This product reimplements, in Rust, the inference pipeline of Laya
  (https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya), Copyright Convai Innovations,
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Question rendering, sequence
  layout, calibration and result formatting follow that package so answers are
  identical; no code from it is vendored here. The Python package is used only by
  the scripts in scripts/ to produce reference fixtures for tests.

  The model checkpoints this engine runs (convaiinnovations/laya,
  laya-multilingual, laya-typed-decisions on Hugging Face) are distributed by
  Convai Innovations under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and are not part of
  this repository. Their encoders derive from ModernBERT (Answer.AI / LightOn,
  Apache-2.0) and mmBERT (JHU CLSP, MIT).

runtime/vendor/mlx-sys is mlx-sys 0.6.0 (https://github.com/oxiglade/mlx-rs, MIT OR Apache-2.0)
with a patched build.rs that can link a prebuilt MLX.

runtime/crates/laya-mlx/src/kernels/mlx holds 5 Metal headers copied unchanged from MLX 0.32.2
(https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx), Copyright 2023 Apple Inc., licensed under the MIT License
(see runtime/crates/laya-mlx/src/kernels/mlx/LICENSE).

bench/workloads are built from the typed-decisions benchmark states; bench/reference holds
answers from upstream Laya (PyTorch, fp32, CPU) on those workloads.
